) records purged permanently?

· Records, version snapshots, favorite reminders: physically deleted, unrecoverable;
· Disk: not one byte touched — downloaded content and backup folders all stay as they are (if a content folder is still on disk it will later show up as an "orphan folder" on the [Exceptions] page, where you can handle it);
· After a successful purge steamcmd is automatically told to forget the entry — it will never assemble it back, so revival is cut at the root (the original ledger file is auto-backed up; skipped while steamcmd is running, run it later on the [Cleared Ledger Management] page);
· Invalid archives and operation logs are kept as historical evidence.

